import Foundation

// Oct 7 -- LETTERHEAD rack data (generated offline, then frozen here).
//
// Each entry: a common six-letter BASE word (the rack is its letters,
// shuffled) -> the common English words of 3-6 letters that can be spelled
// from that rack (each letter used at most as often as it appears). Built
// from a word-frequency list (common words only), cross-checked against a
// dictionary's lower-case entries (so proper nouns and most abbreviations are
// out), with contractions, names and a handful of unsuitable words removed by
// hand. Every rack has at least 14 such words, including 2+ of 5-6 letters.
//
// This list is what "words you missed" is drawn from. It is deliberately the
// COMMON words, not every possible English word: players may also find other
// valid words, which the game accepts through the iOS spell checker
// (WoidleSystemDictionary) -- those simply aren't in the reveal list.

